LICENSE RECOMMENDATIONS
========================

Based on your requirements (portfolio showcase, future
commercialization, retained authorship), here are three
options ranked by suitability:

1. ★ CUSTOM COMMERCIAL LICENSE (RECOMMENDED)
────────────────────────────────────────────
   Best for: Full control over commercialization

   Advantages:
   • You retain all rights and can sell/license the software
   • Attribution to JAI GUDIVADA / JAI VERSE is preserved
   • Prevents others from reselling without your permission
   • Allows portfolio showcase with attribution
   • Flexible — you can grant exceptions on a case-by-case
     basis

   This is the file above. It gives you maximum flexibility
   for future commercialization while protecting your
   authorship.

2. MIT LICENSE
──────────────
   Best for: Open-source community adoption

   Advantages:
   • Permissive — anyone can use, modify, and distribute
   • Simple and well-understood
   • Good for community contributions

   Disadvantages:
   • Others can sell your software without paying you
   • No restriction on removing attribution in modified
     versions (though the copyright notice must remain)
   • Less suitable if you plan to monetize the software

   If you choose MIT, the copyright line should read:
     Copyright (c) 2026 JAI VERSE (JAI GUDIVADA)

3. PROPRIETARY / ALL RIGHTS RESERVED
─────────────────────────────────────
   Best for: Complete restriction

   Advantages:
   • Full copyright protection
   • No one can use, copy, or distribute without permission

   Disadvantages:
   • Prevents portfolio showcase without explicit permission
   • No community contributions
   • Harder to share with potential employers/clients
   • Cannot be open-sourced

